---
title: Troubleshooting
order: 90
tags: [help]
---

## Broken fragment links

Symptom: `quaydoc check` reports `broken-fragment`, or clicking a table of
contents entry never scrolls the page.

Start from the page and heading the report names. Rebuild that page and
open the rendered HTML: find the heading you expected to jump to, read the
`id` attribute it actually has, then compare it with the fragment written
in the link. When the two spellings differ, the link cannot resolve.

## Missing pages

`missing-page` means a path link points at a source file that does not
build a page. Check the spelling, and remember that `draft: true` files
build nothing.

## Duplicate ids

`duplicate-id` means one page assigns the same id twice — usually two
headings with the same title. The first keeps the base id; the second gets
a `-2` suffix.

## Nothing renders

Check the front matter: a missing closing `---` swallows the whole page.
Run `python3 -m quaydoc.cli check site` and read `.quay-check.txt`.
